According to a report by Intel Market Research, global car recycling market size was valued at USD 45.0 billion in 2025. The market will expand from USD 46.2 billion in 2026 to USD 80.3 billion by 2034, exhibiting a CAGR of 6.6 % during the forecast period.
Car recycling refers to the systematic dismantling of end of life vehicles (ELVs) to recover ferrous and non ferrous metals such as steel and aluminum, as well as plastics, glass and hazardous components like batteries and fluids; the process reduces raw material demand and mitigates landfill waste.
